  "question": {
    "text": "At room temperature $\\left(27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\right)$, the resistance of a heating element is $50 \\Omega$. The temperature coefficient of the material is $2.4 \\times 10^{-4}{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$. The temperature of the element, when its resistance is $62 \\Omega$, is _____ ${ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1027",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{R}_0(1+\\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T}) \\\\ & 62=50\\left[1+2.4 \\times 10^{-4} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}\\right] \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{T}=1000^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{T}-27^{\\circ}=1000^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} \\\\ & \\mathrm{T}=1027^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}